(Fractional Laser-Primed Photothermal Nanoparticle Therapy Versus Ultrasonic Delivery for) Tj
T*
(Acne Treatment: Clinical and Histological Outcomes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Twenty-four Asian patients with moderate-to-severe acne were randomised to either) Tj
T*
(fractional laser followed by nanoparticle therapy or ultrasound-assisted nanoparticle) Tj
T*
(delivery, with both groups subsequently receiving thermal laser treatment. The fractional-) Tj
T*
(laser-primed group demonstrated clinically visible reductions in all lesion categories,) Tj
T*
(including improvement in existing scarring. Histological specimens showed selective) Tj
T*
(destruction of sebaceous follicles with minimal surrounding dermal injury. The ultrasound-) Tj
T*
(assisted delivery group showed comparable clinical responses. Both approaches were well-) Tj
T*
(tolerated with minimal discomfort during treatment and rapid recovery. No participants) Tj
T*
(developed serious adverse effects. Laboratory testing for systemic gold absorption showed) Tj
T*
(negligible serum or urine levels in both groups. Improvement was evident by clinical) Tj
T*
(assessment at follow-up examination. Photographs documented meaningful reduction in acne) Tj
T*
(burden and surface scarring in both arms, with no significant between-group differences.) Tj
T*
(Participants reported high satisfaction with cosmetic outcomes. These findings support the) Tj
T*
(efficacy and safety of both nanoparticle delivery approaches for acne management. The data) Tj
T*
(suggest that laser-based disruption of the stratum corneum does not substantially enhance) Tj
T*
(therapeutic benefit relative to acoustic delivery in this patient population.) Tj
